  "published": "2026-05-01T09:01:05.703Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "eeCLOUD 4.0.1 refines the V4 Object Graph paradigm and prepares the package for production publication.\n\nHighlights in this release:\n- Object Graph fast-path writes are now routed through the shared SQL engine abstraction instead of PostgreSQL-only core logic.\n- Added batched SQL Object Graph writes for PostgreSQL, MySQL and SQL Server, keeping steady-state WriteObjectData performance close to the Raw JSON path.\n- Added batched Object Graph update handling so UpdateObjectData can convert existing Raw JSON rows in-place and persist child objects without falling back to one write round-trip per nested child.\n- Added optimized Object Graph reads for PostgreSQL, MySQL and SQL Server through the shared engine interface.\n- Preserved Object Graph functional compatibility on eeCACHE; FTP remains explicitly unsupported for Object Graph storage.\n- Improved bootstrap retry behavior so successful auto-created databases and memories no longer leak transient startup errors into successful results.\n- Fixed V4 timing consistency for object reads and updated the test harness so method and wall timings reflect the same measured invocation.\n- Preserved mixed Raw JSON / Object Graph reads, schema evolution, clustered parent reads and object update semantics.\n- Refreshed package metadata and README to reflect the current Raw JSON and Object Graph positioning.",
